// The SOURCE-un-annotated face of `coalesce-nullable-list-element`: the list is a bare
// literal, so inference and not an annotation decides the element's rep. An annotation pins a
// rep, which is why the annotated twin cannot see a defect whose ingredient is inference doing
// the pinning instead — and this template is the one that found D1830.
//
// 44 of its 46 cells are expected to REFUSE today with `union atom has no value box`, at the
// LITERAL rather than the read. It is the standing guard on D1830: a cell that comes back
// SILENT is that gap turning into a miscompile, and a cell that RUNS means D1830 closed.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
const elems = [42, null]
// @@VALUE@@
elems[0] ?? 0
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@FALLBACK@@
0
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
42
// @@VALUE2@@
elems[1] ?? 42
// @@TYPE2@@
i32
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v)
// @@WANT2@@
42
